 "briefing": "# Databricks Pre-Meeting Briefing: 16 October to 15 November 2026\n\n## Research Status\n\nNo sourced developments for Databricks dated 16 October to 15 November 2026 could be verified. Every search across news, product launches, executive hires, and deals returned no usable results, and no primary or secondary source was retrieved. Nothing below is a finding about what happened in the window. The absence of results does not show that nothing happened, so the sections below should be read as coverage gaps, not confirmed quiet periods.\n\n## 1. News\n\nNo verified news items for the window. Coverage from the Databricks newsroom, the Databricks blog, and major tech and financial press (including Reuters, Bloomberg, TechCrunch, and The Information) could not be retrieved.\n\n## 2. Product Launches\n\nNo verified product launches, general availability releases, public previews, open-source releases, or pricing or packaging changes for the window. Release notes, blog posts, and product pages were not successfully retrieved.\n\n## 3. Executive and Key Hires\n\nNo verified executive appointments, departures, or board changes for the window. The Databricks leadership page, official executive profiles, and SEC officer-change filings (Form 8-K) were not successfully retrieved.\n\n## 4. Deals\n\nNo verified acquisitions, partnerships, funding rounds, valuation news, customer wins, or other commercial agreements for the window. Partner announcements and SEC filings were not successfully retrieved.\n\n## Open Questions for the Meeting\n\n1. Which product releases, previews, or pricing changes did Databricks make between mid-October and mid-November 2026, and where are they documented publicly?\n2. Have there been any changes to the executive team, board, or go-to-market leadership since October 2026 that we should factor into our discussions?\n2. Which commercial agreements, customer wins, or funding or partnership developments from the past 30 days should we treat